 "description": "Best for: the facts of one posting, such as \"what does the senior backend job at Stripe require?\" or \"how should I tailor my resume for this role?\". It reads the posting only, never the user's own text.\nReturns: must-haves, nice-to-haves, the level and the words that signal it, terms to mirror, years asked, location, the process and referral facts the posting states, and a short resume tailoring checklist. If the job is not found, it returns job_not_found with the closest open titles.\nInput tips: send company and job, such as {\"company\": \"Stripe\", \"job\": \"Senior Backend Engineer\"}. The job is the applyUrl or exact title; call find_company_jobs first if you do not know either.\nNot for: checking the user's own profile or resume text against a job (use profile_keyword_check).",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "company": {
    "description": "The company name as the user says it, such as \"Stripe\", or its careers page link.",
    "maxLength": 300,
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "job": {
    "description": "The job's applyUrl from find_company_jobs, or its exact title, such as \"Senior Backend Engineer\". Call find_company_jobs first if you know neither.",
    "maxLength": 300,
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "company",
   "job"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
 "name": "job_fit_brief",
